meta {
  name: Reject the whole book placement
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/placements/{{wholeBookPlacementId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "rejected"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq rejected
  res.body.confirmed_by: isUndefined
}

docs {
  The other half of review. A rejected placement stays as a row: it is the
  record that somebody looked at this suggestion and said no, and without it
  the next import proposes the same mapping again with nothing to show that it
  was already considered.

  Rejecting never writes confirmed_by. Confirmation is the only thing that
  field records, and a rejection carrying a confirmer would be read by every
  report as agreement.
}
